    display(HYP_REGISTER)

# %% [markdown]
### 23B.5 Pre-registered protocol for a confirmatory v3.1 (T3)

The protocol is written once (the first execution that reaches this cell) and never overwritten; its SHA-256 is printed so that any later v3.1 run can show it followed the registered plan. Nothing in v3.1 may be tuned on the 2024-2026 block, which is now spent.

# %%
V31_PROTOCOL = [
    ("Status", "Registered after the v3.0 test block was opened. v3.0 results are final; v3.1 is a new study with a new, untouched test period."),
    ("New test period", "Forward data only: decisions from 2026-12-01 until at least 2027-08-31 (about 9 months; longer if possible). No v3.1 choice may use any label from this period; labels are collected by a scheduled job and opened once, after a hashed freeze, as in v3.0."),
    ("Development data", "Training 2016-10 to 2022-12, early stopping and calibration 2023, validation 2024-01 to 2026-08 (the v3.0 test block becomes validation: it is no longer a test)."),
    ("Universe", "The 50 v3.0 stocks plus an extension to S&P 500 members with 10 years of verified hourly bars, including companies that were delisted during the period (survivorship control)."),
    ("Computer vision changes", "(1) A chart encoding that keeps the volatility level: a fixed price scale per stock (log price relative to the 60-session mean, in units of trailing volatility) next to the min-max chart; (2) the vertical-rescale augmentation removed for the volatility head; (3) five seeds per model; mean and spread reported."),
    ("NLP changes", "(1) Five seeds per encoder; (2) layer-wise learning-rate decay, longer warm-up and bias-corrected AdamW for the large encoders (Mosbach et al. 2021); (3) QLoRA fine-tuning of FinGPT; (4) minute-stamped news alongside filings; (5) the text-change and dictionary features of §23B.2 as pre-specified inputs."),
    ("Hypotheses (fixed now)", "P1: the fixed-scale chart model beats the min-max chart model on volatility R-squared. P2: CV beats the strongest numbers-only baseline on direction skill (own shuffled nulls) at 5 and 10 days. P3: technical + text features beat technical + filing-calendar + company columns on volatility. P4: the best combination of networks (chosen on validation) beats the best single network within each modality. P5: filing-day reactions exceed non-filing-day reactions, by form (replication of H7)."),
    ("Primary metrics and tests", "Direction: macro-F1 minus the model's own within-month shuffled null; volatility: R-squared and QLIKE; drawdown: ROC-AUC and Brier skill. Paired month-block bootstrap, 5,000 draws, Holm within each hypothesis family, alpha 0.05. Every baseline of v3.0 (prior, HAR / momentum / trailing volatility, technical LightGBM, per-company base rates, filing calendar) is included."),
    ("Decision rules", "A hypothesis is supported only if its Holm-corrected p is below 0.05 and the interval excludes zero on the new test period. Results are reported whether or not they are supported; no model is added after the freeze."),
    ("Ethics and data", "SEC fair-access policy (declared user agent, at most 8 requests per second), licensed price data used for research only, no personal data, gated model licences respected (Llama 2 Community License), not financial advice."),
]
try:
    _pp = SUB["results"] / "v31_protocol.md"
    if not _pp.exists():
        _pp.write_text("# NEXUS Alpha v3.1 - pre-registered protocol\n\nRegistered (UTC): " + now_utc() + "\n\n" +
                       "\n\n".join(f"## {h_}\n\n{b_}" for h_, b_ in V31_PROTOCOL) + "\n")
    V31_SHA = hashlib.sha256(_pp.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
    V31_REGISTERED = re.search(r"Registered \(UTC\): (\S+)", _pp.read_text()).group(1) if re.search(r"Registered \(UTC\): (\S+)", _pp.read_text()) else "n/a"
    (SUB["results"] / "v31_protocol.json").write_text(json.dumps({"registered_utc": V31_REGISTERED, "sha256": V31_SHA,
                                                                  "sections": [{"heading": h_, "text": b_} for h_, b_ in V31_PROTOCOL]}, indent=1))
    print(f"v3.1 protocol registered {V31_REGISTERED}; SHA-256 {V31_SHA[:16]}")
except Exception as e_:
    failed("phase_a3_protocol", e_)
PHASE_A3 = {"utc": now_utc(), "tables": A3_TABLES, "models": ["cv_combo_best", "nlp_combo_best", "nlpp_combo_best", "fusion_combo_best", "tech_event_lazy", "tech_event_textfeat"]}
(SUB["results"] / "phase_a3_results.json").write_text(json.dumps(PHASE_A3, indent=1, default=str))
tick("23B phase a3")
